    dict(key='14-act-4-figure', kind='figure', title='A boundary is a ceiling: only the overlap is allowed',
         body='boundary',
         narration="Fourth demo: a permissions boundary. [[slnc 400]] On the left, the identity's policy: the wildcard, allow star on star. [[slnc 300]] Twenty five things. [[slnc 600]] In the middle, the boundary. [[slnc 300]] It allows reading: list and get in S 3, and scan, query and get item in Dynamo D B. [[slnc 300]] And it denies the secrets bucket. [[slnc 700]] A request must pass both. [[slnc 300]] On the right, the overlap: the eight things left. [[slnc 300]] List the reports bucket. [[slnc 300]] Read the report file. [[slnc 300]] And get item, query and scan, on the orders and customers tables. [[slnc 700]] Underneath, the counts. [[slnc 300]] Twenty five alone. [[slnc 300]] Eight under the boundary. [[slnc 300]] And the boundary alone: zero. [[slnc 300]] A boundary is a ceiling. [[slnc 300]] It grants nothing."),
    dict(key='15-act-4-1', kind='console', title='Act Four — A permissions boundary',
         body='FOUR. A permissions boundary.\n  THE BOUNDARY AS WRITTEN (a ceiling, not a grant):\n    Allow s3:List*, s3:Get*, dynamodb:Scan, dynamodb:Query,\n      dynamodb:GetItem\n      on *\n    Deny s3:* on shop-secrets/*, shop-secrets\n  THE COUNT (what a stolen key reaches):\n    wildcard alone               25 of 25\n    wildcard under the boundary   8 of 25\n    the boundary alone            0 of 25  <- GRANTS NOTHING\n    admin_with_deny, bounded      8 of 25',
         narration='Here is the output. [[slnc 400]] The boundary as written. [[slnc 400]] Then the counts. [[slnc 300]] The wildcard alone, twenty five. [[slnc 300]] Under the boundary, eight. [[slnc 300]] The boundary alone, zero. [[slnc 300]] And admin with a deny, under the boundary, eight.'),
    dict(key='16-act-4-2', kind='console', title='Act Four — A permissions boundary',
         body='FOUR. (continued)\n  THE 8 THINGS LEFT (wildcard under the boundary):\n    s3:ListBucket on shop-reports\n    s3:GetObject on shop-reports/q3.csv\n    dynamodb:GetItem on table/orders\n    dynamodb:GetItem on table/customers\n    dynamodb:Query on table/orders\n    dynamodb:Query on table/customers\n    dynamodb:Scan on table/orders\n    dynamodb:Scan on table/customers\n  allowed = in a policy AND in the boundary, and never denied',
         narration='These are the eight things left: one list, one read, and three table actions on two tables. [[slnc 500]] A request is allowed only when a policy allows it and the boundary allows it, and nothing denies it.'),
